3 P50 rises to ~2.0%, CQ6-C falls ~8pp into B, and hypothesis (b) falls to ~7. Philippine BPO headcount above 2.1M (versus ~1.7M) independently falsifies the virtual-leg compression and takes hypothesis (b) to ~6.\"} | {\"signpost\":\"US 10-year TIPS yield (FRED DFII10) average for calendar 2031, together with the G7 PPP-GDP-weighted nominal-minus-breakeven aggregate as reconstructible from national index-linked markets.\",\"by_when\":\"Mar 31 2032\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"A US average above 3.0% with the G7 aggregate above 2.4% falsifies my -27bp r* term and takes CQ4 P50 to ~2.5%, CQ5 to ~34 (the MOVE floor shifts to ~100), and CQ6-C up ~6pp. A US average below 1.5% with the aggregate below 1.2% falsifies the +80bp term-premium term, taking CQ4 P50 to ~1.4%, CQ5 to ~18, and CQ6-D up ~6pp.\"}","updateBasis":{"kind":"launch","note":"run1 wave 2 fermi seat, effort 'labor'."}}